      <bpmn:userTask id="W3677_Task5" name="Import Coordinator/Product Compliance Manager obtain the ICC/SOC certificate…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Import Coordinator/Product Compliance Manager obtain the ICC/SOC certificate from BPS upon successful test, verify the certificate scope/quantity/validity, and coordinate ICC sticker issuance (links to W3678) for the certified units
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator / Product Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): Product Compliance Manager
Duration: 2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3677_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3677_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3677_Task6" name="Customs Broker/Import Coordinator use the ICC/SOC certificate to finalize…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Customs Broker/Import Coordinator use the ICC/SOC certificate to finalize customs clearance (links to VS-87) — the BPS certificate is a prerequisite to BOC release of regulated goods — and coordinate delivery to DC (links to VS-04/VS-02.2) and putaway (links to W3678 sticker application)
Responsible (R): Customs Broker / Import Coordinator / DC
Accountable (A): Product Compliance Manager
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3677_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3677_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3677_Task7" name="Import Coordinator/Finance capture the certification cost (BPS fees, testing…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Import Coordinator/Finance capture the certification cost (BPS fees, testing, stickers) into landed cost (links to W144/VS-02.2) and archive the certificate to the ICC register (links to W3672) and technical file (links to W3668) per retention (links to VS-88)
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator / Finance / Records
Accountable (A): Product Compliance Manager
Duration: Per shipment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3677_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3677_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
