    <bpmn:process id="W_W3679" name="W3679. Sample Failure, Re-export &amp; Disposition Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Failed test result (W3676); BPS rejection
Frequency: On failure
Volume: Low frequency; high cost per event
Owner: Product Compliance Manager / Import
Participants: Product Compliance Manager, Import Coordinator, Customs Broker (links to VS-87), Vendor Mgmt (links to VS-03), Finance (links to VS-17), Legal (links to VS-100.3), Quality (links to VS-31), DC (links to VS-04)
Source: workflow W3679 — Sample Failure, Re-export &amp; Disposition Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3679_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3679_Lane1" name="Product Compliance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3679_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3679_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3679_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3679_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3679_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3679_Start3" name="Failed test result (W3676); BPS rejection">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3679_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3679_Task4" name="Product Compliance Manager manage the failed-sample event: confirm the failure…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Product Compliance Manager manage the failed-sample event: confirm the failure against the PNS criterion, place the affected lot on hold/stop-sell (links to W3684), notify BPS, and prevent release to customs/DC pending disposition
Responsible (R): Product Compliance Manager / Import / Quality
Accountable (A): Product Compliance Manager
Duration: On failure</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3679_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3679_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3679_Task5" name="Product Compliance Manager/Import execute the BPS-directed disposition…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Product Compliance Manager/Import execute the BPS-directed disposition: re-export or destruction under DTI supervision (the entire shipment may be affected), manage customs/drawback implications (links to VS-87.2), and coordinate with the vendor on root cause and recovery (links to W3686)
Responsible (R): Product Compliance Manager / Import / Customs Broker / Vendor
Accountable (A): Product Compliance Manager
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3679_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3679_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3679_Task6" name="Product Compliance Manager/Vendor Mgmt drive corrective action (vendor process…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Product Compliance Manager/Vendor Mgmt drive corrective action (vendor process fix, re-test, re-shipment), capture the failure cost (product loss, freight, demurrage, destruction, re-procurement) for vendor recovery (links to W3686), and feed root cause to quality (links to VS-31) and assortment decisions (links to VS-01)
Responsible (R): Product Compliance Manager / Vendor Mgmt / Finance
Accountable (A): Product Compliance Manager
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3679_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3679_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3679_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3679_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3679_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-581 (ensure controlled execution — Import ICC/SOC Clearance, Testing Lab &amp; Sticker Management (PA-117.2).) | - operational: lot segregation and BPS-directed disposition; operational: contract terms and documented root cause
Owner: Product Compliance Manager / Import</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
