    <bpmn:process id="W_W3680" name="W3680. Testing Laboratory Relationship, Accreditation &amp; Cost Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Lab sourcing (W3673); performance review; renewal
Frequency: Per lab + ongoing
Volume: DTI-accredited labs used for regulated-product testing
Owner: Product Compliance Manager / Quality
Participants: Product Compliance Manager, Quality (links to VS-31), Procurement (links to VS-34), Import Coordinator, Vendor Mgmt (links to VS-03), Vendor Scorecard (links to VS-67), Finance (links to VS-17.4)
Source: workflow W3680 — Testing Laboratory Relationship, Accreditation &amp; Cost Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3680_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3680_Lane1" name="Product Compliance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3680_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3680_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3680_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3680_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3680_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3680_Start3" name="Lab sourcing (W3673); performance review; renewal">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3680_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3680_Task4" name="Product Compliance Manager/Quality/Procurement qualify and select…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Product Compliance Manager/Quality/Procurement qualify and select DTI-accredited testing laboratories: confirm BPS accreditation scope (the PNS test methods covered), capacity, turnaround, cost, and location; maintain the approved-lab list and diversify to avoid bottleneck
Responsible (R): Product Compliance Manager / Quality / Procurement
Accountable (A): Product Compliance Manager
Duration: Per lab</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3680_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3680_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3680_Task5" name="Product Compliance Manager/Quality manage the lab relationship and performance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Product Compliance Manager/Quality manage the lab relationship and performance: turnaround SLA, test-quality, pricing, and capacity planning against the regulated-import pipeline (links to W3673); route tests to optimize cycle-time and cost
Responsible (R): Product Compliance Manager / Quality
Accountable (A): Product Compliance Manager
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3680_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3680_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3680_Task6" name="Product Compliance Manager/Finance manage testing cost: benchmark per-test cost…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Product Compliance Manager/Finance manage testing cost: benchmark per-test cost across labs, consolidate volume for discount, allocate testing cost to landed cost (links to W144), and publish testing cost/cycle-time analytics to program reporting (links to W3685) and merchandising (links to VS-01)
Responsible (R): Product Compliance Manager / Finance / Quality
Accountable (A): Product Compliance Manager
Duration: Ongoing + quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3680_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3680_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3680_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3680_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3680_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-581 (ensure controlled execution — Import ICC/SOC Clearance, Testing Lab &amp; Sticker Management (PA-117.2).) | - operational: diversification and capacity planning; operational: accreditation monitoring and backup labs
Owner: Product Compliance Manager / Quality</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
